  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-search-order",
      "text": "**English** · [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nA visual configuration panel for DSH's official `web_search` tool. Manage search sources, their priority and common settings directly in DSH."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- Add, remove and reorder search sources. If a source fails, the next one is tried automatically.\n- Configure API keys, endpoints and source-specific parameters in the panel.\n- Choose the text depth for DeepSeek official search: Default (short snippet), +summary (long summary) or +content (page body).\n\nBuilt-in sources: DeepSeek official search, DeepSeek Messages, Exa, Tavily, Perplexity and Brave Search. Sources from other installed search plugins can also be added."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Requires DSH `>=0.2.0-rc.1 <0.3.0`, with `dsh` and `pnpm` on `PATH`.\n\nInstall directly from GitHub:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:Breeze-04/dsh-search-order\n```\n\nFrom a local checkout or extracted release directory:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add <absolute-path-to-plugin-directory>\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "1. Open **Settings → Plugins → dsh-search-order** in DSH.\n2. Add sources and arrange them in priority order, from top to bottom.\n3. Use the gear button on each source to configure its key, endpoint and parameters.\n\nChanges are saved immediately and apply to the next search. The default order is **DeepSeek official search → DeepSeek Messages**."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "API keys are managed by DSH's credential store; source-specific environment variables are also supported. DeepSeek Messages can use the DSH account login.\n\n[Development](CONTRIBUTING.md) · [Third-party notices](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md) · [MIT License](LICENSE)"
    }
  ],
  "skipped": []
